# --- ALE fork additions (surgical; each verified via a controlled getAllFilesFromDir probe) ---
# Our test runs more tools (snpeff/cnvkit/manta/tiddit/hc) and fork-specific features than upstream's
# default test, producing non-deterministic files upstream's patterns don't cover. Excluded from CONTENT
# (stable_path) only — every file still appears as a NAME in stable_name. Deterministic ALE deliverables
# (cn_matrices CSVs, cnvkit .cnr/.cns/.bed, tiddit stats TSVs, README) are KEPT.
# cnvkit plain VCF (##fileDate) + diagram PDF (creation timestamp):
variant_calling/**/*.cnvcall.vcf
variant_calling/**/*.md-diagram.pdf
# fork-only hard-filtered split VCFs + index:
variant_calling_filtered/**/*.vcf.{gz,gz.tbi}
# snpeff QC stats (embed a Date stamp) — our reports/snpeff/<tool>/<sample>/ is one level deeper
# than upstream's reports/snpeff/*/ pattern:
reports/snpeff/**/*_snpEff.csv
reports/snpeff/**/snpEff_summary.html
# mosdepth regions.bed.gz: CONTENT is deterministic (verified by zcat diff), but the bgzf
# BLOCK FRAMING varies with mosdepth's thread scheduling, so the compressed md5 flips
# between runs (caught 2026-08-31; the pre-SVDB snapshot had recorded one byte-variant).
reports/mosdepth/**/*.bed.gz
reports/mosdepth/**/*.bed.gz.csi
# samtools stats (embeds the cram path / command line):
reports/samtools/**/*.stats
# igv-reports dashboard HTML (non-deterministic sessionDictionary) — nested AND top-level
# (** matches subdirs but not direct children of mutation_reports/):
mutation_reports/**/*.html
mutation_reports/*.html
# bundled VCFs + index (gzip framing):
mutation_reports/**/*.vcf.{gz,gz.tbi}
# plain-VCF SVDB merge inputs (data/sv_svdb/merge_inputs/): header ##fileDate is the
# caller's run time, so md5 is run-dependent — assert names only, like the .vcf.gz above
mutation_reports/**/*.vcf
# fork-only TABIX publish dir (bgzipped VCF + index):
tabix/**
# snpeff MultiQC tables (SnpEff version-dependent):
multiqc/multiqc_data/*snpeff*.txt
